§ `The principal questions and the conclusions for the Code`

`no previous statement` MEANS `Previous Statement Facts` WITH
    `the previous statement was made in writing or reduced into writing` IS FALSE
    `the previous statement was oral` IS FALSE
    `the previous statement is relevant to matters in question in the proceeding in which the witness is cross-examined` IS FALSE
    `the previous statement is inconsistent with the witness's present testimony` IS FALSE
    `the witness does not distinctly admit that the witness made the oral statement` IS FALSE
    `it is intended to contradict the witness by the writing` IS FALSE
    `the witness's attention was called, before the writing is proved, to the parts of it which are to be used for contradicting the witness` IS FALSE
    `the circumstances of the supposed oral statement, sufficient to designate the particular occasion, were mentioned to the witness and the witness was asked whether the witness made it` IS FALSE
    `the previous inconsistent or contradictory statement is proved by virtue of section 147` IS FALSE
    `direct oral evidence of the fact stated by the maker would be admissible` IS FALSE
    `the witness is cross-examined on a document used by the witness to refresh the witness's memory` IS FALSE
    `the document is received in evidence by virtue of section 147(4)` IS FALSE
    `a written law or rule of practice requires the evidence given by the maker of the statement to be corroborated or regulates the manner in which it is treated if uncorroborated` IS FALSE
    `the witness whom it is intended to corroborate has given testimony` IS FALSE
    `the former statement relates to the same fact` IS FALSE
    `the former statement was made at or about the time when the fact took place, or before an authority legally competent to investigate the fact` IS FALSE

`no impeachment` MEANS `Impeachment and Corroboration Facts` WITH
    `the credit of the witness is impeached by the adverse party` IS FALSE
    `the credit of the witness is impeached by the party who calls the witness with the consent of the court` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is of persons who testify that from their knowledge of the witness they believe the witness unworthy of credit` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is proof that the witness has been bribed, has accepted the offer of a bribe, or has received another corrupt inducement to give evidence` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is proof of former statements inconsistent with a part of the witness's evidence which is liable to be contradicted` IS FALSE
    `the witness gives evidence of a relevant fact and is questioned as to other circumstances observed at or near the time or place of that fact` IS FALSE
    `the court is of the opinion that those circumstances, if proved, would corroborate the testimony of the witness as to the relevant fact` IS FALSE
    `the proceedings are criminal proceedings and the corroborating evidence is the evidence of another witness` IS FALSE
    `a statement relevant under section 32 or 33 has been proved` IS FALSE
    `the statement is admissible by virtue of section 32(1)` IS FALSE
    `the statement is admissible by virtue of section 32(1)(b)` IS FALSE
    `the evidence to be corroborated was given by the maker of the statement` IS FALSE
    `the evidence to be corroborated was given by the person who originally supplied the information from which the statement was made` IS FALSE

`no hearsay ground` MEANS `Hearsay Facts` WITH
    `the statement is of a relevant fact` IS FALSE
    `the statement was made by a person, whether orally, in a document or otherwise` IS FALSE
    `the statement is a protest, greeting or other verbal utterance and the relevant fact is one the utterance implies` IS FALSE
    `the statement is made by a person as to the cause of that person's death, or as to a circumstance of the transaction that resulted in that person's death` IS FALSE
    `the cause of that person's death comes into question` IS FALSE
    `the statement was made by a person in the ordinary course of a trade, business, profession or other occupation` IS FALSE
    `the statement is made in a document that is, or forms part of, a record compiled by a person acting in the ordinary course of a trade, business, profession or other occupation on information supplied by other persons` IS FALSE
    `the statement is against the pecuniary or proprietary interest of the person making it` IS FALSE
    `the statement, if true, would expose or would have exposed the maker to a criminal prosecution or to a suit for damages` IS FALSE
    `the statement gives the opinion of the maker as to the existence of a public right or custom or a matter of public or general interest` IS FALSE
    `the maker would have been likely to be aware of the existence of that right, custom or matter if it existed` IS FALSE
    `the statement was made before any controversy as to that right, custom or matter had arisen` IS FALSE
    `the statement relates to the existence of a relationship by blood, marriage or adoption between persons as to whose relationship the maker had special means of knowledge` IS FALSE
    `the statement was made before the question in dispute was raised` IS FALSE
    `the statement relates to the existence of a relationship by blood, marriage or adoption between deceased persons and is made in a will or deed relating to the affairs of their family, in a family pedigree, or upon a tombstone, family portrait or other thing on which such statements are usually made` IS FALSE
    `the statement is contained in a deed or other document relating to a transaction mentioned in section 13(a)` IS FALSE
    `the statement was made by a number of persons and expressed feelings or impressions on their part relevant to the matter in question` IS FALSE
    `the maker is compellable to give evidence on behalf of the party desiring to give the statement in evidence` IS FALSE
    `the maker attends or is brought before the court` IS FALSE
    `the maker refuses to be sworn or affirmed` IS FALSE
    `the maker is sworn or affirmed but refuses to give any evidence` IS FALSE
    `the maker is dead` IS FALSE
    `the maker is unfit because of a bodily or mental condition to attend as a witness` IS FALSE
    `despite reasonable efforts to locate the maker, the maker cannot be found, whether within or outside Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the maker is outside Singapore and it is not practicable to secure the maker's attendance` IS FALSE
    `the maker is competent but not compellable to give evidence on behalf of the party desiring to give the statement in evidence, and refuses to do so` IS FALSE
    `the parties to the proceedings agree that for the purpose of those proceedings the statement may be given in evidence` IS FALSE
    `the oral statement was put by another person, at the maker's request, into writing at the time or reasonably soon afterwards` IS FALSE
    `the court is of the view that it would not be in the interests of justice to treat the statement as relevant` IS FALSE
    `the kind of proceedings` IS `criminal proceedings`
    `the notice requirements and other conditions prescribed in the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules are complied with` IS FALSE
    `the statement is to be given in evidence on the prosecution's behalf` IS FALSE
    `when the agreement was made the accused or a co-accused was represented by an advocate` IS FALSE
    `the agreement was made during proceedings before an examining Magistrate conducting a committal hearing under Division 2 of Part 10 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 as in force immediately before 17 September 2018` IS FALSE
    `the proceedings are before the General Division of the High Court or arise out of proceedings before it` IS FALSE

`no former testimony` MEANS `Former Testimony Facts` WITH
    `the evidence was given by a witness in a judicial proceeding or before a person authorised by law to take it` IS FALSE
    `the witness is dead` IS FALSE
    `the witness cannot be found` IS FALSE
    `the witness is incapable of giving evidence` IS FALSE
    `the witness is kept out of the way by the adverse party` IS FALSE
    `the court considers that the witness's presence cannot be obtained without an amount of delay or expense that is unreasonable in the circumstances` IS FALSE
    `the proceeding was between the same parties or their representatives in interest` IS FALSE
    `the earlier proceeding was a criminal trial or inquiry and the later proceeding is between the same prosecutor and accused` IS FALSE
    `the adverse party in the first proceeding had the right and opportunity to cross-examine` IS FALSE
    `the questions in issue were substantially the same in the first as in the second proceeding` IS FALSE

`no admission` MEANS `Admission Facts` WITH
    `the statement is oral or documentary` IS FALSE
    `the statement suggests an inference as to a fact in issue or a relevant fact` IS FALSE
    `the maker is a person accused of an offence` IS FALSE
    `the statement states or suggests the inference that the maker committed that offence` IS FALSE
    `the maker is a party to the proceeding` IS FALSE
    `the maker is an agent of a party whom the court regards in the circumstances as expressly or impliedly authorised by the party to make the statement` IS FALSE
    `the maker is a party suing or sued in a representative character` IS FALSE
    `the maker held that representative character when making the statement` IS FALSE
    `the maker has a proprietary or pecuniary interest in the subject matter of the proceeding and made the statement in that character` IS FALSE
    `the maker is a person from whom a party to the suit derived the party's interest in the subject matter` IS FALSE
    `the statement was made during the continuance of the maker's interest` IS FALSE
    `the maker's position or liability must be proved as against a party to the suit` IS FALSE
    `the statement would be relevant as against the maker in relation to the position or liability in a suit brought by or against the maker` IS FALSE
    `the maker occupied the position or was subject to the liability when making the statement` IS FALSE
    `the maker is a person to whom a party to the suit has expressly referred for information in reference to the matter in dispute` IS FALSE
    `the admission is sought to be proved against the maker or the maker's representative in interest` IS FALSE
    `the admission is sought to be proved by or on behalf of the maker or the maker's representative in interest` IS FALSE
    `the admission is of such a nature that, if the maker were dead, it would be relevant between third persons under section 32` IS FALSE
    `the admission is a statement of a state of mind or body, relevant or in issue, made at or about the time it existed and accompanied by conduct rendering its falsehood improbable` IS FALSE
    `the admission is relevant otherwise than as an admission` IS FALSE
    `the admission is an oral admission as to the contents of a document` IS FALSE
    `the party proposing to prove it shows that the party is entitled to give secondary evidence of the contents of the document` IS FALSE
    `the genuineness of a document produced is in question` IS FALSE
    `the proceedings are civil proceedings` IS FALSE
    `the admission was made upon an express condition that evidence of it is not to be given` IS FALSE
    `the admission was made upon circumstances from which the court can infer that the parties agreed together that evidence of it should not be given` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is of a matter that an advocate or solicitor may be compelled to give evidence of under section 128` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is of a matter that a legal counsel in an entity may be compelled to give evidence of under section 128A` IS FALSE

`no expert opinion` MEANS `Opinion Facts` WITH
    `the court is likely to derive assistance from an opinion upon a point of scientific, technical or other specialised knowledge` IS FALSE
    `the person has scientific, technical or other specialised knowledge based on training, study or experience` IS FALSE
    `the court is of the view that it would not be in the interests of justice to treat the opinion as relevant` IS FALSE
    `the fact supports or is inconsistent with a relevant opinion of an expert` IS FALSE
    `the court has to form an opinion as to the person by whom a document was written or signed` IS FALSE
    `the opinion is that of a person acquainted with the handwriting of the person by whom the document is supposed to be written or signed` IS FALSE
    `the opinioner has seen that person write, or has received documents purporting to be written by that person in answer to documents written by the opinioner or under the opinioner's authority, or documents purporting to be written by that person have been habitually submitted to the opinioner in the ordinary course of business` IS FALSE
    `the court has to form an opinion as to the existence of a general custom or right` IS FALSE
    `the opinion is that of a person who would be likely to know of its existence if it existed` IS FALSE
    `the court has to form an opinion as to the usages and tenets of a body of men or family, the constitution and government of a religious or charitable foundation, or the meaning of words or terms used in particular districts or by particular classes of people` IS FALSE
    `the opinion is that of a person having special means of knowledge on the subject` IS FALSE
    `the court has to form an opinion as to the relationship of one person to another` IS FALSE
    `the opinion is expressed by conduct of a person who as a member of the family or otherwise has special means of knowledge on the subject` IS FALSE
    `the prosecution is under section 6A of the Women's Charter 1961 and the question is whether there was a marriage` IS FALSE
    `the opinion of a living person is relevant` IS FALSE

`no question to the accused` MEANS `Accused Cross-examination Facts` WITH
    `the accused gives evidence in the criminal proceedings` IS FALSE
    `the question tends to reveal that the accused has committed, or has been charged with or convicted or acquitted of, an offence other than the offence charged` IS FALSE
    `the question tends to reveal that the accused is generally or in a particular respect a person of bad disposition or reputation` IS FALSE
    `evidence of the fact is admissible for proving the commission of the offence charged by virtue of section 14 or 15 of the Evidence Act 1893 or another written law` IS FALSE
    `2 or more persons are jointly charged and the evidence of the fact is admissible for the purpose of showing another of the accused to be not guilty` IS FALSE
    `the accused personally or by an advocate asked a witness for the prosecution or for a person jointly charged a question concerning the witness's conduct on an occasion or whether the witness has committed, or been charged with, convicted or acquitted of, an offence` IS FALSE
    `the court is of the opinion that the main purpose of that question was to raise an issue as to the witness's credibility` IS FALSE
    `the court is of the opinion that the question is relevant to the accused's credibility as a witness` IS FALSE
    `the accused has given evidence against a person jointly charged in the same proceedings` IS FALSE
    `the party cross-examining is entitled under section 56 to establish that the accused is a person of bad disposition or reputation` IS FALSE

`a witness contradicted by a written statement` MEANS `Previous Statement Facts` WITH
    `the previous statement was made in writing or reduced into writing` IS TRUE
    `the previous statement was oral` IS FALSE
    `the previous statement is relevant to matters in question in the proceeding in which the witness is cross-examined` IS TRUE
    `the previous statement is inconsistent with the witness's present testimony` IS FALSE
    `the witness does not distinctly admit that the witness made the oral statement` IS FALSE
    `it is intended to contradict the witness by the writing` IS TRUE
    `the witness's attention was called, before the writing is proved, to the parts of it which are to be used for contradicting the witness` IS TRUE
    `the circumstances of the supposed oral statement, sufficient to designate the particular occasion, were mentioned to the witness and the witness was asked whether the witness made it` IS FALSE
    `the previous inconsistent or contradictory statement is proved by virtue of section 147` IS FALSE
    `direct oral evidence of the fact stated by the maker would be admissible` IS TRUE
    `the witness is cross-examined on a document used by the witness to refresh the witness's memory` IS FALSE
    `the document is received in evidence by virtue of section 147(4)` IS FALSE
    `a written law or rule of practice requires the evidence given by the maker of the statement to be corroborated or regulates the manner in which it is treated if uncorroborated` IS FALSE
    `the witness whom it is intended to corroborate has given testimony` IS FALSE
    `the former statement relates to the same fact` IS FALSE
    `the former statement was made at or about the time when the fact took place, or before an authority legally competent to investigate the fact` IS FALSE

`a witness impeached by the adverse party` MEANS `Impeachment and Corroboration Facts` WITH
    `the credit of the witness is impeached by the adverse party` IS TRUE
    `the credit of the witness is impeached by the party who calls the witness with the consent of the court` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is of persons who testify that from their knowledge of the witness they believe the witness unworthy of credit` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is proof that the witness has been bribed, has accepted the offer of a bribe, or has received another corrupt inducement to give evidence` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is proof of former statements inconsistent with a part of the witness's evidence which is liable to be contradicted` IS TRUE
    `the witness gives evidence of a relevant fact and is questioned as to other circumstances observed at or near the time or place of that fact` IS FALSE
    `the court is of the opinion that those circumstances, if proved, would corroborate the testimony of the witness as to the relevant fact` IS FALSE
    `the proceedings are criminal proceedings and the corroborating evidence is the evidence of another witness` IS FALSE
    `a statement relevant under section 32 or 33 has been proved` IS FALSE
    `the statement is admissible by virtue of section 32(1)` IS FALSE
    `the statement is admissible by virtue of section 32(1)(b)` IS FALSE
    `the evidence to be corroborated was given by the maker of the statement` IS FALSE
    `the evidence to be corroborated was given by the person who originally supplied the information from which the statement was made` IS FALSE

`a dying person's statement` MEANS `Hearsay Facts` WITH
    `the statement is of a relevant fact` IS TRUE
    `the statement was made by a person, whether orally, in a document or otherwise` IS TRUE
    `the statement is a protest, greeting or other verbal utterance and the relevant fact is one the utterance implies` IS FALSE
    `the statement is made by a person as to the cause of that person's death, or as to a circumstance of the transaction that resulted in that person's death` IS TRUE
    `the cause of that person's death comes into question` IS TRUE
    `the statement was made by a person in the ordinary course of a trade, business, profession or other occupation` IS FALSE
    `the statement is made in a document that is, or forms part of, a record compiled by a person acting in the ordinary course of a trade, business, profession or other occupation on information supplied by other persons` IS FALSE
    `the statement is against the pecuniary or proprietary interest of the person making it` IS FALSE
    `the statement, if true, would expose or would have exposed the maker to a criminal prosecution or to a suit for damages` IS FALSE
    `the statement gives the opinion of the maker as to the existence of a public right or custom or a matter of public or general interest` IS FALSE
    `the maker would have been likely to be aware of the existence of that right, custom or matter if it existed` IS FALSE
    `the statement was made before any controversy as to that right, custom or matter had arisen` IS FALSE
    `the statement relates to the existence of a relationship by blood, marriage or adoption between persons as to whose relationship the maker had special means of knowledge` IS FALSE
    `the statement was made before the question in dispute was raised` IS FALSE
    `the statement relates to the existence of a relationship by blood, marriage or adoption between deceased persons and is made in a will or deed relating to the affairs of their family, in a family pedigree, or upon a tombstone, family portrait or other thing on which such statements are usually made` IS FALSE
    `the statement is contained in a deed or other document relating to a transaction mentioned in section 13(a)` IS FALSE
    `the statement was made by a number of persons and expressed feelings or impressions on their part relevant to the matter in question` IS FALSE
    `the maker is compellable to give evidence on behalf of the party desiring to give the statement in evidence` IS FALSE
    `the maker attends or is brought before the court` IS FALSE
    `the maker refuses to be sworn or affirmed` IS FALSE
    `the maker is sworn or affirmed but refuses to give any evidence` IS FALSE
    `the maker is dead` IS FALSE
    `the maker is unfit because of a bodily or mental condition to attend as a witness` IS FALSE
    `despite reasonable efforts to locate the maker, the maker cannot be found, whether within or outside Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the maker is outside Singapore and it is not practicable to secure the maker's attendance` IS FALSE
    `the maker is competent but not compellable to give evidence on behalf of the party desiring to give the statement in evidence, and refuses to do so` IS FALSE
    `the parties to the proceedings agree that for the purpose of those proceedings the statement may be given in evidence` IS FALSE
    `the oral statement was put by another person, at the maker's request, into writing at the time or reasonably soon afterwards` IS FALSE
    `the court is of the view that it would not be in the interests of justice to treat the statement as relevant` IS FALSE
    `the kind of proceedings` IS `criminal proceedings`
    `the notice requirements and other conditions prescribed in the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules are complied with` IS FALSE
    `the statement is to be given in evidence on the prosecution's behalf` IS FALSE
    `when the agreement was made the accused or a co-accused was represented by an advocate` IS FALSE
    `the agreement was made during proceedings before an examining Magistrate conducting a committal hearing under Division 2 of Part 10 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 as in force immediately before 17 September 2018` IS FALSE
    `the proceedings are before the General Division of the High Court or arise out of proceedings before it` IS FALSE

`a statement of a person who cannot be found` MEANS `Hearsay Facts` WITH
    `the statement is of a relevant fact` IS TRUE
    `the statement was made by a person, whether orally, in a document or otherwise` IS TRUE
    `the statement is a protest, greeting or other verbal utterance and the relevant fact is one the utterance implies` IS FALSE
    `the statement is made by a person as to the cause of that person's death, or as to a circumstance of the transaction that resulted in that person's death` IS FALSE
    `the cause of that person's death comes into question` IS FALSE
    `the statement was made by a person in the ordinary course of a trade, business, profession or other occupation` IS FALSE
    `the statement is made in a document that is, or forms part of, a record compiled by a person acting in the ordinary course of a trade, business, profession or other occupation on information supplied by other persons` IS FALSE
    `the statement is against the pecuniary or proprietary interest of the person making it` IS FALSE
    `the statement, if true, would expose or would have exposed the maker to a criminal prosecution or to a suit for damages` IS FALSE
    `the statement gives the opinion of the maker as to the existence of a public right or custom or a matter of public or general interest` IS FALSE
    `the maker would have been likely to be aware of the existence of that right, custom or matter if it existed` IS FALSE
    `the statement was made before any controversy as to that right, custom or matter had arisen` IS FALSE
    `the statement relates to the existence of a relationship by blood, marriage or adoption between persons as to whose relationship the maker had special means of knowledge` IS FALSE
    `the statement was made before the question in dispute was raised` IS FALSE
    `the statement relates to the existence of a relationship by blood, marriage or adoption between deceased persons and is made in a will or deed relating to the affairs of their family, in a family pedigree, or upon a tombstone, family portrait or other thing on which such statements are usually made` IS FALSE
    `the statement is contained in a deed or other document relating to a transaction mentioned in section 13(a)` IS FALSE
    `the statement was made by a number of persons and expressed feelings or impressions on their part relevant to the matter in question` IS FALSE
    `the maker is compellable to give evidence on behalf of the party desiring to give the statement in evidence` IS FALSE
    `the maker attends or is brought before the court` IS FALSE
    `the maker refuses to be sworn or affirmed` IS FALSE
    `the maker is sworn or affirmed but refuses to give any evidence` IS FALSE
    `the maker is dead` IS FALSE
    `the maker is unfit because of a bodily or mental condition to attend as a witness` IS FALSE
    `despite reasonable efforts to locate the maker, the maker cannot be found, whether within or outside Singapore` IS TRUE
    `the maker is outside Singapore and it is not practicable to secure the maker's attendance` IS FALSE
    `the maker is competent but not compellable to give evidence on behalf of the party desiring to give the statement in evidence, and refuses to do so` IS FALSE
    `the parties to the proceedings agree that for the purpose of those proceedings the statement may be given in evidence` IS FALSE
    `the oral statement was put by another person, at the maker's request, into writing at the time or reasonably soon afterwards` IS FALSE
    `the court is of the view that it would not be in the interests of justice to treat the statement as relevant` IS FALSE
    `the kind of proceedings` IS `criminal proceedings`
    `the notice requirements and other conditions prescribed in the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules are complied with` IS FALSE
    `the statement is to be given in evidence on the prosecution's behalf` IS FALSE
    `when the agreement was made the accused or a co-accused was represented by an advocate` IS FALSE
    `the agreement was made during proceedings before an examining Magistrate conducting a committal hearing under Division 2 of Part 10 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 as in force immediately before 17 September 2018` IS FALSE
    `the proceedings are before the General Division of the High Court or arise out of proceedings before it` IS FALSE

`an expert whose help the court needs` MEANS `Opinion Facts` WITH
    `the court is likely to derive assistance from an opinion upon a point of scientific, technical or other specialised knowledge` IS TRUE
    `the person has scientific, technical or other specialised knowledge based on training, study or experience` IS TRUE
    `the court is of the view that it would not be in the interests of justice to treat the opinion as relevant` IS FALSE
    `the fact supports or is inconsistent with a relevant opinion of an expert` IS FALSE
    `the court has to form an opinion as to the person by whom a document was written or signed` IS FALSE
    `the opinion is that of a person acquainted with the handwriting of the person by whom the document is supposed to be written or signed` IS FALSE
    `the opinioner has seen that person write, or has received documents purporting to be written by that person in answer to documents written by the opinioner or under the opinioner's authority, or documents purporting to be written by that person have been habitually submitted to the opinioner in the ordinary course of business` IS FALSE
    `the court has to form an opinion as to the existence of a general custom or right` IS FALSE
    `the opinion is that of a person who would be likely to know of its existence if it existed` IS FALSE
    `the court has to form an opinion as to the usages and tenets of a body of men or family, the constitution and government of a religious or charitable foundation, or the meaning of words or terms used in particular districts or by particular classes of people` IS FALSE
    `the opinion is that of a person having special means of knowledge on the subject` IS FALSE
    `the court has to form an opinion as to the relationship of one person to another` IS FALSE
    `the opinion is expressed by conduct of a person who as a member of the family or otherwise has special means of knowledge on the subject` IS FALSE
    `the prosecution is under section 6A of the Women's Charter 1961 and the question is whether there was a marriage` IS FALSE
    `the opinion of a living person is relevant` IS FALSE

`a question about the accused's other offences` MEANS `Accused Cross-examination Facts` WITH
    `the accused gives evidence in the criminal proceedings` IS TRUE
    `the question tends to reveal that the accused has committed, or has been charged with or convicted or acquitted of, an offence other than the offence charged` IS TRUE
    `the question tends to reveal that the accused is generally or in a particular respect a person of bad disposition or reputation` IS FALSE
    `evidence of the fact is admissible for proving the commission of the offence charged by virtue of section 14 or 15 of the Evidence Act 1893 or another written law` IS FALSE
    `2 or more persons are jointly charged and the evidence of the fact is admissible for the purpose of showing another of the accused to be not guilty` IS FALSE
    `the accused personally or by an advocate asked a witness for the prosecution or for a person jointly charged a question concerning the witness's conduct on an occasion or whether the witness has committed, or been charged with, convicted or acquitted of, an offence` IS FALSE
    `the court is of the opinion that the main purpose of that question was to raise an issue as to the witness's credibility` IS FALSE
    `the court is of the opinion that the question is relevant to the accused's credibility as a witness` IS FALSE
    `the accused has given evidence against a person jointly charged in the same proceedings` IS FALSE
    `the party cross-examining is entitled under section 56 to establish that the accused is a person of bad disposition or reputation` IS FALSE

`a party admitting a fact` MEANS `Admission Facts` WITH
    `the statement is oral or documentary` IS TRUE
    `the statement suggests an inference as to a fact in issue or a relevant fact` IS TRUE
    `the maker is a person accused of an offence` IS FALSE
    `the statement states or suggests the inference that the maker committed that offence` IS FALSE
    `the maker is a party to the proceeding` IS TRUE
    `the maker is an agent of a party whom the court regards in the circumstances as expressly or impliedly authorised by the party to make the statement` IS FALSE
    `the maker is a party suing or sued in a representative character` IS FALSE
    `the maker held that representative character when making the statement` IS FALSE
    `the maker has a proprietary or pecuniary interest in the subject matter of the proceeding and made the statement in that character` IS FALSE
    `the maker is a person from whom a party to the suit derived the party's interest in the subject matter` IS FALSE
    `the statement was made during the continuance of the maker's interest` IS FALSE
    `the maker's position or liability must be proved as against a party to the suit` IS FALSE
    `the statement would be relevant as against the maker in relation to the position or liability in a suit brought by or against the maker` IS FALSE
    `the maker occupied the position or was subject to the liability when making the statement` IS FALSE
    `the maker is a person to whom a party to the suit has expressly referred for information in reference to the matter in dispute` IS FALSE
    `the admission is sought to be proved against the maker or the maker's representative in interest` IS TRUE
    `the admission is sought to be proved by or on behalf of the maker or the maker's representative in interest` IS FALSE
    `the admission is of such a nature that, if the maker were dead, it would be relevant between third persons under section 32` IS FALSE
    `the admission is a statement of a state of mind or body, relevant or in issue, made at or about the time it existed and accompanied by conduct rendering its falsehood improbable` IS FALSE
    `the admission is relevant otherwise than as an admission` IS FALSE
    `the admission is an oral admission as to the contents of a document` IS FALSE
    `the party proposing to prove it shows that the party is entitled to give secondary evidence of the contents of the document` IS FALSE
    `the genuineness of a document produced is in question` IS FALSE
    `the proceedings are civil proceedings` IS FALSE
    `the admission was made upon an express condition that evidence of it is not to be given` IS FALSE
    `the admission was made upon circumstances from which the court can infer that the parties agreed together that evidence of it should not be given` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is of a matter that an advocate or solicitor may be compelled to give evidence of under section 128` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is of a matter that a legal counsel in an entity may be compelled to give evidence of under section 128A` IS FALSE

`empty bundle` MEANS `Evidence Act Fact Bundle` WITH
    `previous statement facts` IS `no previous statement`
    `impeachment and corroboration facts` IS `no impeachment`
    `hearsay facts` IS `no hearsay ground`
    `former testimony facts` IS `no former testimony`
    `admission facts` IS `no admission`
    `opinion facts` IS `no expert opinion`
    `accused cross-examination facts` IS `no question to the accused`

`bundle: contradicted by a writing` MEANS `Evidence Act Fact Bundle` WITH
    `previous statement facts` IS `a witness contradicted by a written statement`
    `impeachment and corroboration facts` IS `no impeachment`
    `hearsay facts` IS `no hearsay ground`
    `former testimony facts` IS `no former testimony`
    `admission facts` IS `no admission`
    `opinion facts` IS `no expert opinion`
    `accused cross-examination facts` IS `no question to the accused`

`bundle: impeached` MEANS `Evidence Act Fact Bundle` WITH
    `previous statement facts` IS `no previous statement`
    `impeachment and corroboration facts` IS `a witness impeached by the adverse party`
    `hearsay facts` IS `no hearsay ground`
    `former testimony facts` IS `no former testimony`
    `admission facts` IS `no admission`
    `opinion facts` IS `no expert opinion`
    `accused cross-examination facts` IS `no question to the accused`

`bundle: dying statement` MEANS `Evidence Act Fact Bundle` WITH
    `previous statement facts` IS `no previous statement`
    `impeachment and corroboration facts` IS `no impeachment`
    `hearsay facts` IS `a dying person's statement`
    `former testimony facts` IS `no former testimony`
    `admission facts` IS `no admission`
    `opinion facts` IS `no expert opinion`
    `accused cross-examination facts` IS `no question to the accused`

`bundle: absent maker` MEANS `Evidence Act Fact Bundle` WITH
    `previous statement facts` IS `no previous statement`
    `impeachment and corroboration facts` IS `no impeachment`
    `hearsay facts` IS `a statement of a person who cannot be found`
    `former testimony facts` IS `no former testimony`
    `admission facts` IS `no admission`
    `opinion facts` IS `no expert opinion`
    `accused cross-examination facts` IS `no question to the accused`

`bundle: expert` MEANS `Evidence Act Fact Bundle` WITH
    `previous statement facts` IS `no previous statement`
    `impeachment and corroboration facts` IS `no impeachment`
    `hearsay facts` IS `no hearsay ground`
    `former testimony facts` IS `no former testimony`
    `admission facts` IS `no admission`
    `opinion facts` IS `an expert whose help the court needs`
    `accused cross-examination facts` IS `no question to the accused`

`bundle: question to the accused` MEANS `Evidence Act Fact Bundle` WITH
    `previous statement facts` IS `no previous statement`
    `impeachment and corroboration facts` IS `no impeachment`
    `hearsay facts` IS `no hearsay ground`
    `former testimony facts` IS `no former testimony`
    `admission facts` IS `no admission`
    `opinion facts` IS `no expert opinion`
    `accused cross-examination facts` IS `a question about the accused's other offences`

`bundle: party admission` MEANS `Evidence Act Fact Bundle` WITH
    `previous statement facts` IS `no previous statement`
    `impeachment and corroboration facts` IS `no impeachment`
    `hearsay facts` IS `no hearsay ground`
    `former testimony facts` IS `no former testimony`
    `admission facts` IS `a party admitting a fact`
    `opinion facts` IS `no expert opinion`
    `accused cross-examination facts` IS `no question to the accused`

