`a fact in issue` MEANS `Relevancy Facts` WITH
    `the fact is a fact in issue` IS TRUE
    `the person offering the evidence is disentitled by a provision of the law relating to civil procedure to prove the fact` IS FALSE
    `the fact forms part of the same transaction as a fact in issue` IS FALSE
    `the fact is the occasion, cause or effect, immediate or otherwise, of a relevant fact or a fact in issue` IS FALSE
    `the fact constitutes the state of things under which a relevant fact or a fact in issue happened` IS FALSE
    `the fact afforded an opportunity for the occurrence or transaction of a relevant fact or a fact in issue` IS FALSE
    `the fact shows or constitutes a motive for a fact in issue or a relevant fact` IS FALSE
    `the fact shows or constitutes a preparation for a fact in issue or a relevant fact` IS FALSE
    `the fact is the conduct of a party or of an agent of a party in reference to the proceeding or to a fact in issue or relevant to it` IS FALSE
    `the fact is the conduct of a person an offence against whom is the subject of the proceeding` IS FALSE
    `the conduct influences or is influenced by a fact in issue or a relevant fact` IS FALSE
    `the fact is a statement` IS FALSE
    `the statement accompanies and explains an act other than a statement` IS FALSE
    `the fact is a statement made to a person, or in the person's presence and hearing, which affects that person's relevant conduct` IS FALSE
    `the fact is necessary to explain or introduce a fact in issue or a relevant fact` IS FALSE
    `the fact supports or rebuts an inference suggested by a fact in issue or a relevant fact` IS FALSE
    `the fact establishes the identity of a thing or person whose identity is relevant` IS FALSE
    `the fact fixes the time or place at which a fact in issue or a relevant fact happened` IS FALSE
    `the fact shows the relation of the parties by whom a fact in issue or a relevant fact was transacted` IS FALSE
    `the fact is necessary for that purpose` IS FALSE
    `there is reasonable ground to believe that 2 or more persons have conspired together to commit an offence or an actionable wrong` IS FALSE
    `the fact is something said, done or written by one of those persons` IS FALSE
    `the fact is in reference to their common intention` IS FALSE
    `the fact came after the time when the intention was first entertained by any one of them` IS FALSE
    `the fact is inconsistent with a fact in issue or a relevant fact` IS FALSE
    `the fact by itself or with other facts makes the existence or non-existence of a fact in issue or a relevant fact highly probable or improbable` IS FALSE
    `damages are claimed in the proceeding` IS FALSE
    `the fact will enable the court to determine the amount of damages that ought to be awarded` IS FALSE
    `the question is as to the existence of a right or custom` IS FALSE
    `the fact is a transaction by which the right or custom was created, claimed, modified, recognised, asserted or denied, or which was inconsistent with its existence` IS FALSE
    `the fact is a particular instance in which the right or custom was claimed, recognised or exercised, or in which its exercise was disputed, asserted or departed from` IS FALSE
    `the fact shows the existence of a state of mind, or of a state of body or bodily feeling` IS FALSE
    `that state of mind, body or bodily feeling is in issue or relevant` IS FALSE
    `the fact shows the state of mind in reference to the particular matter in question and not generally` IS FALSE
    `the fact is the previous commission by the accused of an offence that is relevant within section 14` IS FALSE
    `the fact is the previous conviction of the accused for that offence` IS FALSE
    `there is a question whether an act was accidental or intentional or done with a particular knowledge or intention` IS FALSE
    `the act formed part of a series of similar occurrences in each of which the person doing the act was concerned` IS FALSE
    `there is a question whether a particular act was done` IS FALSE
    `the fact is the existence of a course of business according to which the act naturally would have been done` IS FALSE
    `the fact is declared relevant by another provision of the Act` IS FALSE
    `a fact that must be proved before the evidence is admissible has been proved, or the party has undertaken to prove it and the court is satisfied with the undertaking` IS FALSE
    `evidence of the fact is admissible only upon proof of some other fact` IS FALSE

`a fact in no way relevant` MEANS `Relevancy Facts` WITH
    `the fact is a fact in issue` IS FALSE
    `the person offering the evidence is disentitled by a provision of the law relating to civil procedure to prove the fact` IS FALSE
    `the fact forms part of the same transaction as a fact in issue` IS FALSE
    `the fact is the occasion, cause or effect, immediate or otherwise, of a relevant fact or a fact in issue` IS FALSE
    `the fact constitutes the state of things under which a relevant fact or a fact in issue happened` IS FALSE
    `the fact afforded an opportunity for the occurrence or transaction of a relevant fact or a fact in issue` IS FALSE
    `the fact shows or constitutes a motive for a fact in issue or a relevant fact` IS FALSE
    `the fact shows or constitutes a preparation for a fact in issue or a relevant fact` IS FALSE
    `the fact is the conduct of a party or of an agent of a party in reference to the proceeding or to a fact in issue or relevant to it` IS FALSE
    `the fact is the conduct of a person an offence against whom is the subject of the proceeding` IS FALSE
    `the conduct influences or is influenced by a fact in issue or a relevant fact` IS FALSE
    `the fact is a statement` IS FALSE
    `the statement accompanies and explains an act other than a statement` IS FALSE
    `the fact is a statement made to a person, or in the person's presence and hearing, which affects that person's relevant conduct` IS FALSE
    `the fact is necessary to explain or introduce a fact in issue or a relevant fact` IS FALSE
    `the fact supports or rebuts an inference suggested by a fact in issue or a relevant fact` IS FALSE
    `the fact establishes the identity of a thing or person whose identity is relevant` IS FALSE
    `the fact fixes the time or place at which a fact in issue or a relevant fact happened` IS FALSE
    `the fact shows the relation of the parties by whom a fact in issue or a relevant fact was transacted` IS FALSE
    `the fact is necessary for that purpose` IS FALSE
    `there is reasonable ground to believe that 2 or more persons have conspired together to commit an offence or an actionable wrong` IS FALSE
    `the fact is something said, done or written by one of those persons` IS FALSE
    `the fact is in reference to their common intention` IS FALSE
    `the fact came after the time when the intention was first entertained by any one of them` IS FALSE
    `the fact is inconsistent with a fact in issue or a relevant fact` IS FALSE
    `the fact by itself or with other facts makes the existence or non-existence of a fact in issue or a relevant fact highly probable or improbable` IS FALSE
    `damages are claimed in the proceeding` IS FALSE
    `the fact will enable the court to determine the amount of damages that ought to be awarded` IS FALSE
    `the question is as to the existence of a right or custom` IS FALSE
    `the fact is a transaction by which the right or custom was created, claimed, modified, recognised, asserted or denied, or which was inconsistent with its existence` IS FALSE
    `the fact is a particular instance in which the right or custom was claimed, recognised or exercised, or in which its exercise was disputed, asserted or departed from` IS FALSE
    `the fact shows the existence of a state of mind, or of a state of body or bodily feeling` IS FALSE
    `that state of mind, body or bodily feeling is in issue or relevant` IS FALSE
    `the fact shows the state of mind in reference to the particular matter in question and not generally` IS FALSE
    `the fact is the previous commission by the accused of an offence that is relevant within section 14` IS FALSE
    `the fact is the previous conviction of the accused for that offence` IS FALSE
    `there is a question whether an act was accidental or intentional or done with a particular knowledge or intention` IS FALSE
    `the act formed part of a series of similar occurrences in each of which the person doing the act was concerned` IS FALSE
    `there is a question whether a particular act was done` IS FALSE
    `the fact is the existence of a course of business according to which the act naturally would have been done` IS FALSE
    `the fact is declared relevant by another provision of the Act` IS FALSE
    `a fact that must be proved before the evidence is admissible has been proved, or the party has undertaken to prove it and the court is satisfied with the undertaking` IS FALSE
    `evidence of the fact is admissible only upon proof of some other fact` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `may evidence be given of the fact` `a fact in issue`

#ASSERT NOT `may evidence be given of the fact` `a fact in no way relevant`

`a lost original` MEANS `Document Facts` WITH
    `the document itself is produced for the inspection of the court` IS FALSE
    `the document was executed in several parts and the thing produced is one of the parts` IS FALSE
    `the document was executed in counterpart and the thing produced is a counterpart offered against a party who executed it` IS FALSE
    `the thing produced is one of a number of documents all made by one uniform process, offered as evidence of the contents of another of them` IS FALSE
    `the thing produced and the document it is offered to prove are copies of a common original` IS FALSE
    `the thing produced is a copy of a document in the form of an electronic record and is shown to reflect that document accurately` IS FALSE
    `the thing produced is a certified copy given under the provisions of the Act` IS FALSE
    `the thing produced is a copy made from the original by a technical process that in itself ensures the accuracy of the copy, or a copy compared with such a copy` IS FALSE
    `the thing produced is a copy made from or compared with the original` IS FALSE
    `the thing produced is a counterpart offered against a party who did not execute it` IS FALSE
    `the thing produced is an oral account of the contents given by a person who has himself or herself seen the document` IS FALSE
    `the original is shown or appears to be in the possession or power of the person against whom the document is sought to be proved` IS FALSE
    `the original is shown or appears to be in the possession or power of a person out of reach of or not subject to the process of the court` IS FALSE
    `the original is shown or appears to be in the possession or power of a person legally bound to produce it` IS FALSE
    `after the notice mentioned in section 68 that person does not produce it` IS FALSE
    `the existence, condition or contents of the original have been proved to be admitted in writing by the person against whom it is proved or by that person's representative in interest` IS FALSE
    `the original has been destroyed or lost` IS TRUE
    `the party offering evidence of its contents cannot, for a reason not arising from the party's own default or neglect, produce it in reasonable time` IS FALSE
    `the original is of such a nature as not to be easily movable` IS FALSE
    `the original is a public document within the meaning of section 76` IS FALSE
    `the original is a document of which a certified copy is permitted by the Act or by another law in force in Singapore to be given in evidence` IS FALSE
    `the originals consist of numerous accounts or other documents that cannot conveniently be examined in court and the fact to be proved is the general result of the whole collection` IS FALSE
    `the party proposing to give secondary evidence has previously given the party in possession, or that party's solicitor, the notice to produce prescribed by law or, if none is prescribed, the notice the court considers reasonable` IS FALSE
    `the document to be proved is itself a notice` IS FALSE
    `from the nature of the case the adverse party must know that the adverse party will be required to produce it` IS FALSE
    `it appears or is proved that the adverse party has obtained possession of the original by fraud or force` IS FALSE
    `the adverse party or the adverse party's agent has the original in court` IS FALSE
    `the adverse party or the adverse party's agent has admitted the loss of the document` IS FALSE
    `the person in possession of the document is out of reach of or not subject to the process of the court` IS FALSE
    `the court thinks fit to dispense with the notice` IS FALSE
    `the document is alleged to be signed or written wholly or in part by a person` IS FALSE
    `the document is an electronic record or electronic signature to which the Electronic Transactions Act 2010 applies` IS FALSE
    `the signature or handwriting has been proved to be in that person's handwriting` IS FALSE

`an original in the court` MEANS `Document Facts` WITH
    `the document itself is produced for the inspection of the court` IS TRUE
    `the document was executed in several parts and the thing produced is one of the parts` IS FALSE
    `the document was executed in counterpart and the thing produced is a counterpart offered against a party who executed it` IS FALSE
    `the thing produced is one of a number of documents all made by one uniform process, offered as evidence of the contents of another of them` IS FALSE
    `the thing produced and the document it is offered to prove are copies of a common original` IS FALSE
    `the thing produced is a copy of a document in the form of an electronic record and is shown to reflect that document accurately` IS FALSE
    `the thing produced is a certified copy given under the provisions of the Act` IS FALSE
    `the thing produced is a copy made from the original by a technical process that in itself ensures the accuracy of the copy, or a copy compared with such a copy` IS FALSE
    `the thing produced is a copy made from or compared with the original` IS FALSE
    `the thing produced is a counterpart offered against a party who did not execute it` IS FALSE
    `the thing produced is an oral account of the contents given by a person who has himself or herself seen the document` IS FALSE
    `the original is shown or appears to be in the possession or power of the person against whom the document is sought to be proved` IS FALSE
    `the original is shown or appears to be in the possession or power of a person out of reach of or not subject to the process of the court` IS FALSE
    `the original is shown or appears to be in the possession or power of a person legally bound to produce it` IS FALSE
    `after the notice mentioned in section 68 that person does not produce it` IS FALSE
    `the existence, condition or contents of the original have been proved to be admitted in writing by the person against whom it is proved or by that person's representative in interest` IS FALSE
    `the original has been destroyed or lost` IS FALSE
    `the party offering evidence of its contents cannot, for a reason not arising from the party's own default or neglect, produce it in reasonable time` IS FALSE
    `the original is of such a nature as not to be easily movable` IS FALSE
    `the original is a public document within the meaning of section 76` IS FALSE
    `the original is a document of which a certified copy is permitted by the Act or by another law in force in Singapore to be given in evidence` IS FALSE
    `the originals consist of numerous accounts or other documents that cannot conveniently be examined in court and the fact to be proved is the general result of the whole collection` IS FALSE
    `the party proposing to give secondary evidence has previously given the party in possession, or that party's solicitor, the notice to produce prescribed by law or, if none is prescribed, the notice the court considers reasonable` IS FALSE
    `the document to be proved is itself a notice` IS FALSE
    `from the nature of the case the adverse party must know that the adverse party will be required to produce it` IS FALSE
    `it appears or is proved that the adverse party has obtained possession of the original by fraud or force` IS FALSE
    `the adverse party or the adverse party's agent has the original in court` IS FALSE
    `the adverse party or the adverse party's agent has admitted the loss of the document` IS FALSE
    `the person in possession of the document is out of reach of or not subject to the process of the court` IS FALSE
    `the court thinks fit to dispense with the notice` IS FALSE
    `the document is alleged to be signed or written wholly or in part by a person` IS FALSE
    `the document is an electronic record or electronic signature to which the Electronic Transactions Act 2010 applies` IS FALSE
    `the signature or handwriting has been proved to be in that person's handwriting` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `may secondary evidence be given of the document` `a lost original`

#ASSERT NOT `may secondary evidence be given of the document` `an original in the court`

`an accused relying on a Penal Code exception` MEANS `Burden Facts` WITH
    `the party who would fail if no evidence at all were given on either side is the party who asserts the fact` IS FALSE
    `a law provides that the proof of the fact is to lie on a particular person` IS FALSE
    `the fact is necessary to be proved in order to enable a person to give evidence of another fact` IS FALSE
    `the person is accused of an offence` IS TRUE
    `the circumstance brings the case within a general exception in the Penal Code 1871` IS TRUE
    `the circumstance brings the case within a special exception or proviso contained in another part of the Penal Code 1871` IS FALSE
    `the circumstance brings the case within a special exception or proviso contained in a law defining the offence` IS FALSE
    `the fact is especially within the knowledge of a person` IS FALSE
    `the question is whether a person is alive or dead and it is shown that the person was alive within 30 years` IS FALSE
    `the question is whether a person is alive or dead and it is proved that the person has not been heard of for 7 years by those who would naturally have heard of the person if alive` IS FALSE
    `the question is whether persons are partners, landlord and tenant, or principal and agent, and it has been shown that they have been acting as such` IS FALSE
    `the question is whether a person is the owner of a thing of which the person is shown to be in possession` IS FALSE
    `there is a question as to the good faith of a transaction between parties one of whom stands to the other in a position of active confidence` IS FALSE

`a prosecution asserting the offence` MEANS `Burden Facts` WITH
    `the party who would fail if no evidence at all were given on either side is the party who asserts the fact` IS TRUE
    `a law provides that the proof of the fact is to lie on a particular person` IS FALSE
    `the fact is necessary to be proved in order to enable a person to give evidence of another fact` IS FALSE
    `the person is accused of an offence` IS FALSE
    `the circumstance brings the case within a general exception in the Penal Code 1871` IS FALSE
    `the circumstance brings the case within a special exception or proviso contained in another part of the Penal Code 1871` IS FALSE
    `the circumstance brings the case within a special exception or proviso contained in a law defining the offence` IS FALSE
    `the fact is especially within the knowledge of a person` IS FALSE
    `the question is whether a person is alive or dead and it is shown that the person was alive within 30 years` IS FALSE
    `the question is whether a person is alive or dead and it is proved that the person has not been heard of for 7 years by those who would naturally have heard of the person if alive` IS FALSE
    `the question is whether persons are partners, landlord and tenant, or principal and agent, and it has been shown that they have been acting as such` IS FALSE
    `the question is whether a person is the owner of a thing of which the person is shown to be in possession` IS FALSE
    `there is a question as to the good faith of a transaction between parties one of whom stands to the other in a position of active confidence` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `is the burden on the accused under section 107` `an accused relying on a Penal Code exception`

#ASSERT NOT `is the burden on the accused under section 107` `a prosecution asserting the offence`
